In article <1993May7.215544.189@fcom.cc.utah.edu>, holmbeck@cs.weber.edu (Laura Holmbeck) writes:
 > On my machine, a Sun, when one tries to start up nethack,
 >  it gives you the error message and refuses to run:
 > 
 > Too many hacks running now.
 > 
 > 
 > Anyone else get this error? what does it mean?  Is it fixable?
 > 
 > Thanks in advance,
 > -- Laura
Nethack for unix may be compiled in such a way that it limits the number
of users that can play at the same time.  Use the ps command to find
out if other people are playing, (if other people have access to
your machine.)  If no other nethack's are running, then it is a bug.
Perhaps the limit is set to zero, or it could be a problem in the routine
that detects other games.  Take a look at config.h if you have the source.

